# QA M5 BUG (acceptance pass): after a stomp bounce from the Zaunerstollen
# perch the camera climbs to y 0 and the lake is off the screen. D-086
# says the auto-scroll camera stays "between ~20 (a high jump) and 92",
# so every swan, Gelse and regatta trigger is horizontal only. As
# Zuckerschock (qa_m5_wolfgangsee_relaxed's inputs) Resi stomps Gelse #3
# from the perch (row 8): the bounce takes her top to y 35 and the dead
# zone pulls the camera to y 0 by 3710; it stays at 0-2 until 3792 and is
# below 24 until ~3815. At y 0 the screen ends at world y 180: the swim
# water (surface y 192) is not on screen at all, the decks of Traundl C/D
# are cut at the bottom edge. In that time she hops onto the perch bollard
# (jump 3756, lands 3792) and steps off it into the lake (~3800, camera
# y 2-16) without the water she lands in on screen (game-design.md: a
# landing spot is on screen at take-off), and swan #3
# (hitbox y 184-196, home x 2944) is below the screen: it only becomes
# "fully on screen" and telegraphs at 3801 (camera y 16) while she is
# already falling towards its stretch, and it first shows at the very
# bottom-right corner. Same mechanism, milder, on the solver route: a held
# masthead bounce takes the camera to y 20 (3876-3903), the third regatta
# boat's keel (y 204) is below the screen and it starts at 3905 instead of
# its scroll-fixed 3897 (D-074's "scroll-determined, same in every run").
# Expected: in an auto-scroll level the camera never rises so far that
# the water surface leaves the screen (e.g. a top clamp of y >= 24 in the
# scroll zone: water, swans and keels always fully on screen), or the
# perch is placed so that a bounce cannot get there. The shots have no
# goldens: they fail the `goldens` step until the fix is art-director
# APPROVED and accepted.
level  = wolfgangsee
seed   = 1
source = handwritten
expect = deaths=0 no_event=Hurt event=Stomped power=big
shots  = 3725:stomp_bounce_top 3760:perch_hop 3790:drop_into_lake
